{
  "id": "COMPOUND:15061 - PROTEIN:5802",
  "verbalization": "Chaxamycin B is implicated in the regulation of Hs746T through a series of molecular interactions involving a sialyltransferase enzyme. The evidence suggests that Chaxamycin B directly targets the CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a key enzyme in the synthesis of sialic acid. This enzyme is also a target of a complex compound with multiple stereoisomers, which further supports the notion of a broad substrate specificity. The sialyltransferase is ultimately linked to Hs746T, indicating a potential role in metabolic pathways involving sialic acid. Additionally, the presence of Fructose 1,6-Diphosphate as a target of the sialyltransferase adds another layer of complexity, suggesting a possible metabolic regulation pathway. These findings collectively imply that Chaxamycin B may influence Hs746T through a mechanism involving sialic acid synthesis, potentially impacting cellular processes related to glycosylation and metabolic regulation.",
